      {
        "text": "The United States possesses the strongest military in human history.",
        "confidence": 0.98
      },
      {
        "text": "The war in Afghanistan was a bipartisan failure as a policy.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Public opinion does not blame either major political party specifically for the outcome in Afghanistan.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The U.S. military maintains high levels of public respect and support despite policy failures.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The U.S. military consistently fails to achieve its strategic objectives in foreign interventions.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a gap between political leadership and the military in shaping foreign policy outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Many American institutions lack public trust compared to the military.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that national security policy should align with strategic success and public expectations.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "A strong military alone is insufficient to ensure successful foreign policy outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Political leaders are responsible for setting clear strategic objectives for military operations.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The public views military performance through the lens of broader policy effectiveness rather than isolated actions.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Military leaders are expected to operate within a framework set by civilian authorities.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The senator’s dual role as a veteran and policymaker gives them unique credibility on defense issues.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Strategic decision-making in foreign policy requires coordination between political and military actors.",
