    "turn_text": "the reasons the Taliban gained support, especially in the provinces of Afghanistan, is that they deliver justice. But the local government, which is so corrupt, did not. So you had, you know, your neighbor stole your livestock and you went to the local magistrate and tried to get help, you were probably asked to pay a bribe. And you probably never got justice because the guy who stole your cattle or your livestock may have paid off the police officers, right? But if you go to the Calibon, they need out food justice, they cut off the arms. They execute the guys. You get justice. And so if we wanted to nation build, then we should have funded those programs that actually built up a justice system that actually worked. I'll give you an example of one of the things that I was very frustrated about. I went up to Afghanistan in 2014 or 2015. We just women, we just women, congressmen and we went and we met with women in Afghanistan and we met with women police condensed and women, Afghan security forces condensed and we said, how is it going? We got the men out of the room because we said all women, we can talk with each other. We got the male translators out of the room who were really there to watch over them, because those men said, no, no, no. These women don't speak English. We have to translate. We got the men out of the rooms. We were all",
